{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:25:11.071Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"f26067e1c2959c034d8d5b1d8ef4a66483cb80bfa8f2f8ab179e701cd2ae68c7","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@Bettina Kroll, here's the list for Kwame's review, from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- Ticket #4419: `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Open per Moss's cheat sheet. (The Nov 2 digest also cites #4419 for barge slip 7 schedule sync under \"Puget Sound Operations\", so please confirm which issue it is.)\n- Ticket #PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (Gate 4B). From your Dec 2025 cutover recap.\n- Gate 4 chassis pool validation at shift change: the main friction point in the cheat sheet. No ticket number.\n- Berth 2 yard map CSV import bug: mentioned in your cutover recap. No ticket number.\n- Gate 4B printer mapping: mentioned in your cutover recap. No ticket number.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B: engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. No ticket number.\n- Patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift: requested per the Nov 2 digest. No ticket number.\n\nLeft out as Pellow or Saltmarsh: PD-4827, PD-4821, PD-4824, #8812 and the Door 4B scanner issue. I can't see a separate ticket list for either account, so this is what's in the channels and Moss's notes.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
